  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-3).$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-3).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258704/assets/145145a2e750f9eec3d6a010846fcb46fa700878d3cae28e8db315e451273dd2.png)\n\nAs $x$ decreases, the graph oscillates between the values $y=-1$ and $y=1$ indefinitely. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-3)=DNE.\n$$",
